Enables/disables land-cover material tinting

SYNOPSIS

    h.set_materials(True)

DESCRIPTION

Mirrors horizonator_set_materials() in horizonator.h. When
materials_enabled is False (the default), rendering is untinted by land
cover. When True: real land cover, where pre-baked tiles are available
(see landcover.h and build-landcover-tiles.py), falling back to a
procedural elevation/slope classification elsewhere.

ARGUMENTS

- materials_enabled: boolean

RETURNED VALUES

None. Raises an exception on failure.
